6.","title":"Prepositional Phrase of Time","note":"We use the preposition 'in' before years to specify when an event occurred. In this sentence, it functions as a time modifier describing when they started the project."},{"i":3,"focus":"In 1998,","title":"Fronted Time Adverbial","note":"Placing a time phrase at the beginning of a sentence sets the scene first. A comma is typically used after introductory time modifiers."}]},"t2":{"sentences":[{"text":"Larry Page and Sergey Brin met at Stanford University in California.","voice":"voice/reserve-apps-google-began-inside-a/t2-0.m4a","roles":["S","S","S","S","S","V","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":4.68,"voiceJa":"voice/reserve-apps-google-began-inside-a/ja/t2-0.m4a","durJa":5.11,"times":[0.0,0.28,0.68,1.06,1.32,1.9,2.3,2.48,2.82,3.62,3.9]},{"text":"They built a search tool and first called it BackRub.","voice":"voice/reserve-apps-google-began-inside-a/t2-1.m4a","roles":["S","V","O","O","O","M","M","V","O","C"],"dur":2.8,"voiceJa":"voice/reserve-apps-google-began-inside-a/ja/t2-1.m4a","durJa":4.73,"times":[0.0,0.06,0.2,0.36,0.56,0.92,1.3,1.56,1.84,2.0]},{"text":"The software worked very well, so they needed a bigger space.","voice":"voice/reserve-apps-google-began-inside-a/t2-2.m4a","roles":["S","S","V","M","M","M","S","V","O","O","O"],"dur":3.5,"voiceJa":"voice/reserve-apps-google-began-inside-a/ja/t2-2.m4a","durJa":5.5,"times":[0.0,0.04,0.28,0.74,1.04,1.74,1.88,2.12,2.32,2.5,2.72]},{"text":"In September 1998, they moved into a garage in Menlo Park.","voice":"voice/reserve-apps-google-began-inside-a/t2-3.m4a","roles":["M","M","M","S","V","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":4.19,"voiceJa":"voice/reserve-apps-google-began-inside-a/ja/t2-3.m4a","durJa":5.18,"times":[0.0,0.06,0.34,1.88,2.04,2.24,2.52,2.66,3.0,3.4,3.78]},{"text":"Susan Wojcicki owned the garage and charged them 1,700 dollars monthly.","voice":"voice/reserve-apps-google-began-inside-a/t2-4.m4a","roles":["S","S","V","O","O","M","V","O","O","O","M"],"dur":5.07,"voiceJa":"